						<adjective>Man-Seonic</adjective>
						<memberName>Man-Seonist</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>Spiritual Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>Spiritual Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>In a world of weak, simpering men begging for female approval, Heron Biarmi reconnected with masculine power and used it to make a new movement. The women believers wheedled and whined, so Biarmi cast them out of the council of leaders. To consecrate their commitment, Biarmi demanded that believers eat human flesh together at least every week.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>In a world of weak, simpering men begging for female approval, Heron Biarmi reconnected with masculine power and used it to make a new movement. The women believers wheedled and whined, so Biarmi cast them out of the council of leaders. To consecrate their commitment, Biarmi demanded that believers eat human flesh together at least every week.</descriptionTemplate>
